15:["$","div",null,{"className":"article-layout","children":[["$","aside",null,{"className":"article-aside","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mono acid","children":"IN THIS STORY"}],["$","a",null,{"href":"#definition","children":["01 / ","The essential"]}],["$","a",null,{"href":"#analysis","children":["02 / ","The analysis"]}],["$","a",null,{"href":"#practice","children":["03 / ","In practice"]}],["$","a",null,{"href":"#sources","children":["04 / ","Sources & limits"]}],["$","a",null,{"href":"/en/lexicon/","children":["↗ ","The AGD lexicon"]}]]}],["$","article",null,{"className":"article-text","children":[["$","section",null,{"className":"quick-answer","id":"definition","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mono acid","children":"THE TAKEAWAY"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"A frequency test must separate total volume, per-post performance and production load. Higher totals can coexist with weaker individual posts."}]]}],["$","$L18",null,{"a":"$1:props:children:1:props:article","lang":"en"}],"$undefined",["$","section",null,{"id":"analysis","className":"article-prose","children":[["$","p","0",{"children":"Define two realistic cadences with comparable creative quality. Observe coordination costs and undelivered content. Do not conclude from average views alone: the network may seek more qualified visits at a manageable cost. No test result is supplied here."}],["$","p","1",{"children":"A favorable total may also increase team fatigue or correction work. Record those effects in the review instead of treating them as outside the experiment. A suitable cadence depends on the whole system. Sustainable output with readable briefs may be preferable to a production spike that cannot survive the following week. This is an operating tradeoff to evaluate, not an assumption that lower frequency always performs better."}]]}],["$","blockquote",null,{"children":["“","Posting more: more chances or more noise?","”"]}],"$undefined",false,["$","$L18",null,{"a":"$1:props:children:1:props:article","lang":"en","number":2}],["$","section",null,{"id":"practice","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Put it to work."}],["$","ol",null,{"className":"checklist","children":[["$","li","0",{"children":[["$","span",null,{"children":["0",1]}],"Set cadence, duration and primary metric."]}],["$","li","1",{"children":[["$","span",null,{"children":["0",2]}],"Track total cost and per-post outcomes."]}]]}]]}],["$","section",null,{"id":"sources","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"What this does not prove."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"caveat","children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"The limit. "}],"Changing cadence and quality together prevents isolating frequency effects."]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"sources","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mono acid","children":"SOURCES & PROVENANCE"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Original analysis of the AGD framework provided by TokPortal, lexicon and doctrine (2026). Examples are illustrative. No proprietary study or customer outcome is claimed."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"editorial-note","children":["FEEDRAID is an editorial project initiated by TokPortal. That relationship is separate from the evidence behind claims. AI-assisted writing; no fictional journalist identities."," ",["$","a",null,{"href":"/en/about/","children":"Our editorial policy →"}]]}]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"next-read","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mono acid","children":"THE CURRENT CONTINUES"}],["$","h2",null,{"children":["$","a",null,{"href":"/en/read/lab/warming-study/","children":"Warming deserves more than an anecdote."}]}],["$","a",null,{"href":"/en/read/lab/warming-study/","className":"read-link","children":["Next article"," ↗"]}]]}]]}],["$","aside",null,{"className":"article-aside right-aside","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mono muted","children":"CONNECTED IDEAS"}],[["$","a","063",{"href":"/en/read/lab/warming-study/","children":["Warming protocol"," ↗"]}],["$","a","061",{"href":"/en/read/lab/posting-time-myth/","children":["Posting-time myth"," ↗"]}],["$","a","001",{"href":"/en/read/doctrine/distribution-is-the-moat/","children":["Account-Generated Distribution"," ↗"]}]]]}]]}]
16:["$","section",null,{"className":"related-grid","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"section-heading","children":["$","h2",null,{"children":"Other currents."}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"article-grid","children":[["$","$L19","063",{"a":"$1:props:children:1:props:next","lang":"en"}],["$","$L19","061",{"a":"$1:props:children:1:props:previous","lang":"en"}],["$","$L19","001",{"a":{"id":"001","slug":"distribution-is-the-moat","category":"doctrine","term":"Account-Generated Distribution","kind":"essay","image":"distribution-is-the-moat","tier":"canonical","evidence":"editorial","sources":[],"related":["account-isolation","content-isolation","content-saturation"],"en":{"title":"Content is cheap. Distribution isn’t.","dek":"Everyone can produce. Almost nobody knows how to distribute. Welcome to the other side of the iceberg.","point":"Account-Generated Distribution (AGD) organizes differentiated social accounts as organic distribution infrastructure. More accounts only make strategic sense when audiences, voices and creative work also differ.","body":["The pitch fits in a browser tab: one generator, a few prompts, fifty videos. The problem starts after export. Who watches? Why should that person stop at this account instead of the next one? Production has a button. Distribution still needs a reason to exist.","A brand account is often asked to reassure, sell, entertain, recruit and explain. Every post negotiates with the others. AGD separates those jobs. One account explores student frustrations; another challenges work habits; a third demonstrates a product in context. One company, three editorial promises.","The trap is reading this architecture as a volume recipe. Thirty accounts running the same edit do not represent thirty ideas. They mostly multiply coordination, repetition and unanswered questions. Diversification lives in what a viewer receives, not in the number of rows in a spreadsheet.","AGD is a proposed framework drawn from the TokPortal blueprint, not an academic consensus or a reach guarantee. Its value depends on the experiments it helps run. The useful question is whether a network reveals something that one account would hide. Can the signal be connected to an angle, an audience or a format?","Build a small network whose differences you can explain. Document the failures alongside the breakout posts. And keep a commercial measure next to views: somebody enjoying your edit does not necessarily have a problem your product solves."],"action":["Write a different editorial promise for each account.","Attach each post to a hypothesis and an audience.","Measure by cohort, then inspect qualified visits."],"trap":"A clone network can increase output without adding a single perspective.","quote":"The next advantage is knowing where an idea deserves to live.","stories":[{"id":"brief","title":"The idea in three screens.","slides":[{"label":"THE SIGNAL","title":"The next advantage is knowing where an idea deserves to live.","text":"Everyone can produce. Almost nobody knows how to distribute. Welcome to the other side of the iceberg.","media":"/images/iceberg.jpg"},{"label":"THE CONCEPT","title":"Account-Generated Distribution","text":"Account-Generated Distribution (AGD) organizes differentiated social accounts as organic distribution infrastructure. More accounts only make strategic sense when audiences, voices and creative work also differ.","media":"/images/iceberg.jpg"},{"label":"THE OTHER SIDE","title":"What can mislead.","text":"A clone network can increase output without adding a single perspective.","media":"/images/iceberg.jpg"}]},{"id":"practice","title":"From concept to practice.","slides":[{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 1","title":"Write a different editorial promise for each account.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/iceberg.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 2","title":"Attach each post to a hypothesis and an audience.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/iceberg.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 3","title":"Measure by cohort, then inspect qualified visits.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/iceberg.jpg"}]}]},"video":{"src":"/video/below-the-surface.mp4","poster":"/images/iceberg.jpg","caption":{"en":"Below the surface — animated original illustration. No audio."},"tracks":{"en":"/video/intro-en.vtt"}},"schemaVersion":1,"publishedAt":"2026-09-08T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T17:06:44.287Z","author":"feedraid-editorial","media":{"kind":"illustration","src":"/images/iceberg.jpg","width":1536,"height":1024,"alt":{"en":"Night iceberg with a green submerged mass, a metaphor for unseen distribution."},"credit":"FEEDRAID Studio","provenance":"Original AI-generated editorial illustration created for this publication on September 8, 2026. Not a documentary photograph.","source":"https://naybu256.github.io/images/iceberg.jpg","license":"Original artwork","licenseUrl":"https://naybu256.github.io/en/about/#images"}},"lang":"en"}]]}]]}]
